    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441-a1">

                <pb facs="1508" n="1350" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1350"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of State to
                        Minister Collier</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-06-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 1, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: His Majesty, the King, my august
                    sovereign, before whom I had the honor to place the contents of the polite note
                    of yesterday’s date which your excellency addressed to me, has been pleased to
                    command me to beg you to thank the President and the Government of the United
                    States for the congratulations which were extended to His Majesty, as well as to
                    Her Majesty the <pb facs="1509" n="1351" xml:id="pg1351"/> Queen, for having
                    escaped unharmed from the criminal attempt of which they might have been
                    victims, and also to express to your excellency his gratitude for your personal
                    share in these congratulations.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this opportunity to reiterate to your excellency the assurances
                    of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. de Ojeda</hi>.<lb/>P. A. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Under Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
